1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Every body needs a hero.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Osmosis Jones is a adventure, animation, action film directed by Bobby Farrelly.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
A white blood cell policeman, with the help of a cold pill, must stop a
deadly virus from destroying the human they live in, Frank.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Osmosis Jones (voice), played by Chris Rock.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Thrax (voice), played by Laurence Fishburne.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Drix (voice), played by David Hyde Pierce.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Leah (voice), played by Brandy Norwood.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Shane Detorre, played by Elena Franklin.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Frank Detorre, played by Bill Murray.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Osmosis Jones is a 2001 American live-action/animated buddy cop action comedy
film directed by the Farrelly brothers and written by Marc Hyman.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
The film stars the voices of Chris Rock, Laurence Fishburne, David Hyde Pierce, Brandy Norwood and
William Shatner, alongside Molly Shannon, Chris Elliott and Bill Murray in live-action roles.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
It combines live-action sequences directed by the Farrelly Brothers
and animated ones directed by Piet Kroon and Tom Sito.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
It follows the titular protagonist, an anthropomorphic white blood cell police officer, as he teams up with a
cold pill to protect his unhealthy human host from a deadly virus he unintentionally contracted.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
The film premiered on August 7, 2001, and was
released theatrically three days later.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
It received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the worldbuilding, animation, story and voice performances,
but criticized the inconsistent tone of the live-action portions and overusag of gross-out humor.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film was also a commercial failure, grossing $14
million worldwide against a $70 million budget.

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Despite the poor financial response, the film garnered success on home video and was followed by an animated television
series Ozzy & Drix, which aired on Kids' WB for two seasons and twenty-six episodes from 2002 to 2004.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film explores themes of cold, flu, lethal virus, construction worker.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
